# Course Evaluations

=== layout: one-panel

# Course Evaluations

@body

- Hi Students,
- You will be receiving an email to complete [course evaluations]{color=red} for your courses.
- I want to encourage you to complete them, they are our [primary source for evaluating faculty performance]{color=red}.
- Your opinion does matter; it can help determine who gets salary raises, and a string of negative evaluations can get a professor replaced.
- Further, I appreciate getting [your feedback]{color=red} in an anonymous way. It helps me [improve the courses]{color=red} I teach.
- Thanks, Dr. Voss

=== layout: one-panel

# Course Evaluations

@body

- When the IDEA Student Ratings of Instruction survey opens, complete it by the published deadline.
- It can take up to 5-10 minutes to complete the Course Evaluation
- Surveys are open and available for students to complete by accessing the following link\:
  - [https\://roosevelt.campuslabs.com/eval-home/](https://roosevelt.campuslabs.com/eval-home/)
  - Students may log in with their RU Net ID and password.

=== layout: one-panel

# Final Exam Extra Time

@body

- I have decided to link student evaluation completions to extra time on the final exam.
  - Normally\: 50 questions = 75 minutes
- Completing the student evaluation adds up to an extra 20 minutes for each exam part.
  - If all students complete their evaluations, the total time could reach up to 95 minutes for the 50 questions.

